# Header rules for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets (copied to build/).
# Rules apply in this order; a section first unsets (`! Header`) what it sets differently.

# Every page of the suite – one policy for all of them (decided by the user, 2026-11-27): pages change without
# reloading, and a tab keeps the headers of the page it loaded first. So what any tool needs is allowed everywhere:
# the P2P relays (wss:), connected servers (https:, localhost), previews, media, fonts and workers from blob:, and
# screen, microphone and camera (Screen Capture; the browser still asks). What a page really does is the code's
# matter (the catalog of free fonts is reached only from Fonts, and only when the user searches it).
# One origin holds every file, key and paired device: always over HTTPS (HSTS, this host only – subdomains are the
# domain owner's matter), no other site keeps a handle on our windows (COOP) or embeds our files (CORP).
# `scripts/csp.ts` replaces `'unsafe-inline'` by the hashes of the pages' own inline scripts and adds one section per
# group of pages (`/files*`, `/help*` …) with the same policy and that group's hashes – one line for all would be
# longer than Cloudflare takes. A new tool needs no entry here.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(self), display-capture=(self), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self' blob: data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data: wss: https: http://localhost:* http://127.0.0.1:*; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Build files: file names contain a hash – cached permanently. A worker runs under the policy of its own script:
# PDF.js decodes images and runs form scripts (QuickJS) in its workers with WebAssembly, so scripts may compile it;
# pages keep theirs. One block only – rules of the same path are merged at the first one's place,
# before `/*` would add its policy (two policies: both apply, WebAssembly stays forbidden)
/_app/immutable/*
  ! Content-Security-Policy
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# (the sections of the page groups are added here by `scripts/csp.ts`)

# p2p-node (packages/p2p-node): the starters fetch version.json to find updates, people pipe the install scripts
# into a shell – always fresh, scripts as text
/p2p-node/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/p2p-node/install.sh
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

/p2p-node/install.ps1
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

# Always revalidate the Service Worker and the manifests so new versions get through
/service-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.de.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*/manifest.de.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
